## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/cache.html
- Summary (EN): Builds an in-memory cache for each input so expensive operations play back faster, storing frames so inputs need not be recooked. Works for layers, geometry and VDBs. Available since version 21.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud cache conserve en mémoire les images de ses entrées pour accélérer une opération coûteuse, au prix de la RAM et de la VRAM.

- Inputs meaning: ["input#: the source layer to cache (layers, geometry or VDBs)"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Clear Cache", "meaning": "Erases all cached data and forces new results to cook"}, {"name": "Reload Playbar Range", "meaning": "Caches all frames of the current playbar range"}, {"name": "Max Frames", "meaning": "Maximum number of stored frames; lower saves memory but may slow playback away from key frames"}, {"name": "Clear Cache when Change Upstream", "meaning": "On by default; clears the cache when upstream changes, time-based changes excepted"}, {"name": "Output #", "meaning": "Names the output; non-blank names are kept as placeholders when wires are removed"}]

- Caveats: ["Increases RAM and VRAM usage", "Recomputing can sometimes be faster than caching", "Does not store upstream parameter settings", "The page recommends Stash COP to save inputs without cooking them"]

